    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.square_clustering - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.square_clustering.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.square_clustering()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate the square clustering coefficient of every node.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.square_clustering()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate the square clustering coefficient of every node.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.square_clustering()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Calculate the square clustering coefficient of every node.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCalculate the square clustering coefficient of every node.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L37286-L37372){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.square_clustering(\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Square clustering](../assets/graphs/square-clustering.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A 2 by 3 grid, two squares side by side, has no triangles, so the ordinary clustering coefficient, listed in the last column, is 0 for every node. Square clustering sees the squares: the corners A, C, D and F score 0.50, and the middle nodes B and E 0.33, since one of their three neighbor pairs closes no square.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe ordinary clustering coefficient counts triangles; square clustering (Lind,\nGonzález & Herrmann, 2005) counts *squares*: for each pair of a node's neighbors, it\nasks whether they share another neighbor, closing a four-cycle through the node. It\npicks up local cohesion that triangles miss entirely, which matters in bipartite\nnetworks (customers and products, authors and papers), where triangles are impossible\nbut squares are common, and in grid-like or spatial networks.\n\nThe score is the number of squares through the node divided by the number of possible\nsquares, as in NetworkX's `square_clustering()`. Nodes with fewer than two neighbors\nscore `0`. Self-loops are ignored; on a directed graph, neighbors are the nodes a node\npoints to.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute to store scores in. If `None` (default), uses\n    `\"square_clustering\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    scores as a node attribute and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, float], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: a dictionary mapping node IDs to scores in `[0, 1]`.\n    If `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~clustering_coefficient`) \n\n:   Clustering by triangles.\n\n[](`~generalized_degree`) \n\n:   Each node's edges by how many triangles they lie in.\n\n[](`~edge_clustering_coefficient`) \n\n:   Clustering of each edge, by triangles or squares.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA 4-cycle has no triangles, so its ordinary clustering is 0 everywhere, but every node\nsits on its one square:\n\n::: {#cc3d81e4 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nsquare = ec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(4).square_clustering()\nsquare.clustering_coefficient()\n\nsquare.get_node_df().select(\n    \"label\", \"clustering_coefficient\", \"square_clustering\"\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (4, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>clustering_coefficient</th><th>square_clustering</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>f64</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;1&quot;</td><td>0.0</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;2&quot;</td><td>0.0</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;3&quot;</td><td>0.0</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;4&quot;</td><td>0.0</td><td>1.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Who could cover for whom\n\n`teams()` links the 8 workers of a made-up software team to the 8 tasks of a release that\neach can do. Edges only run between a worker and a task, so there are no triangles, but\ntwo workers who can both do two tasks close a square. Kofi scores 1: every pair of Kofi's\ntasks, Database, DevOps and Security, is a pair that Omar can do as well. Mei and Luis\nscore 0, since no one shares two of their tasks:\n\n::: {#90b9c067 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam = ec.teams().square_clustering()\n\n(\n    team.get_node_df()\n    .filter(side=\"worker\")\n    .sort(\"square_clustering\", descending=True)\n    .select(\"label\", \"role\", \"degree\", \"square_clustering\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (8, 4)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>role</th><th>degree</th><th>square_clustering</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>i64</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Kofi&quot;</td><td>&quot;Engineer&quot;</td><td>3</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Priya&quot;</td><td>&quot;Engineer&quot;</td><td>3</td><td>0.272727</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Tom&quot;</td><td>&quot;Engineer&quot;</td><td>3</td><td>0.272727</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Omar&quot;</td><td>&quot;Engineer&quot;</td><td>4</td><td>0.25</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Sara&quot;</td><td>&quot;Writer&quot;</td><td>2</td><td>0.25</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Hana&quot;</td><td>&quot;Tester&quot;</td><td>2</td><td>0.25</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Mei&quot;</td><td>&quot;Designer&quot;</td><td>2</td><td>0.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Luis&quot;</td><td>&quot;Designer&quot;</td><td>2</td><td>0.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe tasks that only Omar and Kofi can do score highest after Kofi:\n\n::: {#e05a5ae5 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam.layout_bipartite(align=\"horizontal\", aspect_ratio=0.4).plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"square_clustering\", label_by=\"label\",\n    height=300,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"